sults/153005"} "1896"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/153130"} "1906"] ". The distance was 100 km."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The team road race reverted to the format used in 1924-28, with four riders on each team, and the best three times to count towards the team time. " [:a {:href "/athletes/13887"} "Robert Charpentier"] " won the individual and led France to victory in the team race. Charpentier won three gold medals in Berlin, as he also won on the track, helping France win the " [:a {:href "/results/153521"} "team pursuit"] "."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/153541"} "Road Race, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "10 August 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "99"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/153542"} "Road Race, Team, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "10 August 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "88"] "\n" [:td {} "22"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {}] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n99 (99/0)\n"] "\n" [:td {:class "border-top"} "\n28 (28/0)\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n\n" [:h2 {} "Medals"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] "\n" [:th {:colspan "2"} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {:class "top"} [:a {:href "/results/153541"} "Road Race, Individual, Men"]] "\n" [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} [:a {:href "/athletes/13887"} "Robert Charpentier"]] [:td {:style "vertical-align: top"} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazo